00:44:41.037 --> 00:44:43.477
- They do, the key idea is

00:44:43.477 --> 00:44:47.652
that multi universe theories
don't come in a single flavor.

00:44:47.652 --> 00:44:48.721
There are various versions.

00:44:48.721 --> 00:44:50.316
And the one that you're referring to now--

00:44:50.316 --> 00:44:51.661
- These are competing theoretical ideas.

00:44:51.661 --> 00:44:53.267
- Actually some people think they're

00:44:53.267 --> 00:44:54.890
the same theory in disguise.

00:44:54.890 --> 00:44:55.723
- [Neil] Okay.

00:44:55.723 --> 00:44:57.950
- You know, so in quantum
mechanics, you have this idea

00:44:57.950 --> 00:44:59.930
that the equations only
predict the probability

00:44:59.930 --> 00:45:01.286
for one outcome or another.

00:45:01.286 --> 00:45:03.891
Like an electron has a
40% chance of being here

00:45:03.891 --> 00:45:05.640
and a 60% chance of being here.

00:45:05.640 --> 00:45:07.089
And the question is, when you measure

00:45:07.089 --> 00:45:08.912
the electron and you find it over here,

00:45:08.912 --> 00:45:11.945
what happened to the other possibility?

00:45:11.945 --> 00:45:13.545
And one of the notions that came out

00:45:13.545 --> 00:45:16.805
of the 1950s is that
that other possibility

00:45:16.805 --> 00:45:19.275
is just as real as the one you witnessed.

00:45:19.275 --> 00:45:21.508
It's simply taking place in another world,

00:45:21.508 --> 00:45:23.330
another universe parallel to yours.

00:45:23.330 --> 00:45:26.245
And there's a version of
you in that world measuring

00:45:26.245 --> 00:45:28.533
that electron and seeing
it at that position,

00:45:28.533 --> 00:45:31.396
thinking there's a unique
outcome from your experiment

00:45:31.396 --> 00:45:33.295
but you're completely wrong
because there are two of you

00:45:33.295 --> 00:45:34.642
each having that thought.

00:45:34.642 --> 00:45:35.475
There are multiple worlds.

00:45:35.475 --> 00:45:36.551
- Calm down, calm down, calm down.

00:45:36.551 --> 00:45:37.384
- Okay.

00:45:37.384 --> 00:45:39.515
